abstract: >-
  SYNTC-AI generates synthetic tropical cyclone catalogues for the Philippine
  Area of Responsibility. Track propagation and intensity evolution are learned
  as conditional densities from the IBTrACS Western North Pacific record
  (1977-2023), replacing the hand-tuned parameterisations of its predecessor
  SynTC. Terrain-dependent wind decay, central pressure, radius of maximum wind
  and the radial wind profile are taken from published relations and used
  unchanged. On held-out years the learned track propagator improves track
  density correlation over a STORM-style binned autoregression from 0.845 to
  0.887.
keywords:
  - tropical cyclone
  - synthetic storm generator
  - Philippine Area of Responsibility
  - western North Pacific
  - mixture density network
  - hazard assessment
